  "finding": "Most traced proof latency increase lies in the BitZ forest outside measured grinding loops. The forest delta is positive for every seed. Integer folds, column packing, power tables and forest grinding are essentially unchanged.",
  "limitations": [
    "Tracing raises absolute runtimes and may change relative costs; these traces are diagnostic and do not replace the untraced qualification or confirmation benchmarks.",
    "Four input seeds and one configuration do not establish universal performance behavior or statistically isolate a causal implementation change.",
    "Stage durations include nested work and logging overhead. Inclusive stage totals overlap; median stage differences need not sum exactly to the median root difference.",
    "The affected bridge/forest/GKR/grinding/transcript source files are byte-identical to the frozen baseline. Localization does not attribute the slowdown to the new serialization helper; compiler/code-layout effects remain an untested hypothesis.",
    "This report describes the original frozen candidate binaries in the command logs, before any subsequent NTT scratch-reduction experiment."
  ],
  "method": "Identify each top-level falcon_algebraic:prove ancestor, exclude its first three occurrences per process, sum elapsed_ms for each full stage path within each remaining trial, take per-process medians, then average four paired-seed medians/deltas. Nested spans are inclusive and must not be added together.",
